Equation of normal to hyperbola at $\left(x_1, y_1\right)$ is

\begin{gathered}
\frac{a^2 x}{x_1}+\frac{b^2 y}{y_1}=a^2+b^2 \\
\therefore \text { At }(6,3), \frac{a^2 x}{6}+\frac{b^2 y}{3}=a^2+b^2
\end{gathered}

It passes throught $(9,0)$.

\begin{aligned}
& \text { Now, } \quad \frac{a^2 \cdot 9}{6}=a^2+b^2 \\
& \Rightarrow \quad \frac{3 a^2}{2}-a^2=b^2 \Rightarrow \frac{a^2}{b^2}=2 \\
& \therefore \quad e^2=1+\frac{b^2}{a^2}=1+\frac{1}{2} \Rightarrow e=\sqrt{\frac{3}{2}}
\end{aligned}

Equation of tangent to hyperbola having slope $m$ is

y=m x+\sqrt{9 m^2-4}

Equation of tangent to circle is

y=m(x-4)+\sqrt{16 m^2+16}

Eqs. (i) and (ii) will be identical for $m=\frac{2}{\sqrt{5}}$ satisfy.
$\therefore$ Equation of common tangent is $2 x-\sqrt{5} y+4=0$

On substituting $\left(\frac{a}{e}, 0\right)$ in $y=-2 x+1$, we get

\begin{aligned}
0 & =-\frac{2 a}{e}+1 \\
\Rightarrow \quad \frac{a}{e} & =\frac{1}{2}
\end{aligned}

Also, $y=-2 x+1$ is tangent to hyperbola

\begin{array}{ll}
\therefore & 1=4 a^2-b^2 \\
\Rightarrow & \frac{1}{a^2}=4-\left(e^2-1\right)
\end{array}

