\begin{array}{ll}
\Rightarrow & \frac{4}{e^2}=5-e^2 \\
\Rightarrow & e^4-5 e^2+4=0 \\
\Rightarrow & \left(e^2-4\right)\left(e^2-1\right)=0 \\
\Rightarrow & e=2, e=1
\end{array}

$e=1$ gives the conic as parabola. But conic is given as hyperbola, hence $e=2$
